# Opt-in hiring-team outreach and post-submit timing fixes
Workstream-ID: lea-08
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/9
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: TODO.md, 2026-07-21 outreach batch and first-live-test fixes
Status: IN_REVIEW
Milestone: Explicitly approved outreach with durable deduplication
Dependencies: None

## Purpose
Track the historical opt-in outreach implementation and its original live
selector-qualification gap. This is not authorization to send messages, and
does not redefine the current product's later outreach/reporting modes.

## Tasks
- [x] Resolve opt-in configuration and CLI overrides.
- [x] Render an approval draft and avoid unsolicited automatic sends.
- [x] Detect recruiter cards, respect unsupported paid-message cases and cap sends.
- [x] Persist draft outcomes and deduplicate by supported contact identity.
- [x] Correct flag gating and preserve the post-submit modal until outreach inspection.
- [x] Add fixture coverage, decision logs and affected documentation.
- [ ] Qualify the source's remaining hiring-card and compose selectors against the target.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Local source records the implementation, fixes and regression results.
- [ ] The explicitly pending live selector cases have evidence, not assumed fixture equivalence.

## Completion evidence
The source records nine outreach fixture cases with a 185-test suite, then
two gating regressions and a 187-test green suite after the timing/flag fixes,
with clean Ruff/Black/mypy checks. It explicitly leaves live selector validation
open. Recorded outreach commits are historical provenance, not a current push
claim. No recruiter names, profile links, message bodies or applicant data
are included, and this migration sends no outreach.

## Completion log
- 2026-07-21: Original outreach implementation and local regression evidence recorded.
- 2026-07-21: First-live-test gating and modal-order fixes recorded.
- 2026-11-06: Kept IN_REVIEW because the original target-qualification gap lacks
  independent closure evidence. Human acceptance and publication remain separate.
